(Grand Definition of Differentiablity) 

Let X ⊆ R^n be open, let f:X -> R^m, and let a ∈ X. 
We say that f is differentiable at a if Df(a) exists and if the function h:R^n -> R^m defined by 

	h(x) = f(a) + Df(a) (x - a)

is a good linear approximation to f near a. 
